From 8bb8a4cfdf3d9ef3b8d4e6e29aa4fb4ed7da5cdb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Tue, 23 Jun 2026 21:57:28 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 03721/11362] [outer-loop] Multi-level L1->L2 wall pinpointed:
 the DEGENERATE L2 GOAL PREDICATE (no_reachable_plan), not the gate

Clean-Qwen (port-8919 gemma confound fixed; verified Qwen3.5-9B served) + per-round instrumentation +
a 4-agent root-cause workflow nail the L1->L2 deepening wall. Decisive baseline (submitted config):

  round1 induce: proposer_ok=True heldout=1.0 ACCEPTED=True plan_len=0 reaches_goal=False cx=no_reachable_plan

The dynamics model PASSES the strict 1.0 gate, but plan_in_model returns no_reachable_plan. With trans=1
the held-out split is ~empty so heldout=1.0 is a VACUOUS pass -> the gate protects/blocks nothing. The
real wall is the L2 GOAL PREDICATE: induced from ZERO L2-win positives (the post-boundary window has no L2
win yet), never verified (the gate checks DYNAMICS only) -> unsatisfiable -> planner can't reach it.

Mechanism (all measured, clean Qwen): the level_up_reinduction is ONE-SHOT (induced=True sticks;
n_induction_attempts=1 every run) + EVIDENCE-STARVED (fires at trans=1) -> the goal induction has no L2
evidence and the gate is vacuous. Lever ablations all plan=0: gate-relax is a NO-OP (gate already passes);
evidence-delay K=25 BACKFIRES (explorer explored_out at ~5 post-L1 transitions, a stall-induction preempts).

Fix priority (NOT the cheap gate knob): (1) dedicated L2-goal-predicate induction passing the L1 win-grid
as a WIN-STATE exemplar + verify the goal is satisfiable before planning; (2) evidence + re-arm paired with
plan_in_model from the current post-L1 grid; (3) proposer retry (secondary). Strategic: for 6/30, first-win
breadth (0.59) likely beats proposer/goal-bound L2 depth.

Artifacts: results/proto_multilevel_diag_real_{baseline,K1gate05,K25gate05}.json; instrumented harness
scripts/experiments/proto_multilevel_diag.py. Parity-safe lever knobs on branch outer-loop/bp35-diag
(commit bfd565922). Root-cause workflow wf_fcab5470-68f.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
